.SH SEE ALSO
.IR radio (3),
.IR attrdb (6),
.IR ndb (6)
.SH VERIFIED
.B "Radiocal under qemu,"
by
.IR tools/radio/radiocaltest.sh :
four rungs, three packets each, none lost, no CRC error, twelve reads,
and the slope arithmetic running.  The model's RSSI is the constant it
was told, so the slope there is 0.000 by construction and the numbers
are silicon's job.  The negative control passes too \-
.B -r
with nothing transmitting reports fewer than three rungs rather than
printing a slope, so the table is not coming from uninitialised arrays.
.PP
.B "Radiocal on two clicker 2 boards,"
forty packets over eight rungs, every one received:
.PP
.EX
	ramp  nominal   got lost crcerr   RSSI mean least most
	  63   +14.0      5    0      0     -30  -31  -30
	  55   +10.0      5    0      0     -33  -33  -33
	  47    +6.0      5    0      0     -37  -37  -37
	  39    +2.0      5    0      0     -41  -41  -41
	  31    -2.0      5    0      0     -45  -45  -45
	  23    -6.0      5    0      0     -48  -49  -48
	  15   -10.0      5    0      0     -53  -53  -53
	   7   -14.0      5    0      0     -56  -56  -56

	slope 0.949 dB of RSSI per dB of transmitter, over 8 rungs
.EE
.PP
.B "Radiocfg on silicon,"
with the board that boots holding the other board's crystal correction:
.PP
.EX
	board2 ppb at boot: -3550
	; radiocfg
	radiocfg: uid 203730395931500800300022 is board2 in /lib/radio
	radiocfg: ppm 60300
	radiocfg: rssioffset -102
	radiocfg: csthr -90
	radiocfg: 3 applied, 0 absent from the entry
.EE
.PP
and each of those three read back out of the stat file.
.PP
.B "And the two together,"
by
.IR tools/radio/calibratedlink.py ,
which is the point of the whole item.  Both boards reset so that the
reading is the kernel's default and not what a previous run left: both
boot at
.B -3550
\- one figure for two boards, which is the bug.  Each runs
.I radiocfg
and they come out 63850ppb apart, which is the 64 parts per million the
crystals are.  Then ten packets, with
.B "the host having written no correction to either board"
and the same frequency string to both: ten received, no CRC error, and
the payload intact.
.PP
.B "Not yet done:"
nothing writes
.B /lib/radio
on the board.  It is in devroot, served read-only out of flash, so a new
measurement means an edit and a reflash.  See
.I doc/radio-plan.ms
item 8's second stage.
.SH BUGS
.I Radiocfg
parses the
.IR attrdb (6)
subset itself rather than using
.IR attrdb (2),
which did not fit: on the stm32f407, with 147456 bytes of Dis pool and
the shell in it, the library found the right entry and then ran out of
heap, from a fresh boot as well.  Its own comment has the measurement.
The file is still
.IR attrdb (6)
and
.IR attrdb (2)
reads it on a host, which is where it is edited.
.PP
The calibration is keyed on the board and not on the radio, because a
CC1120 has no serial number of its own.  That is wrong if a click is
moved between boards, since the crystal belongs to the click; each entry
carries a
.B click
attribute so that a move is recordable rather than silent.
